    "mathematical_reasoning": [
      {
        "audit": "Every probability/range/kernel/root/gap/unit/inverse/polar/global-centering item is an inherited conclusion, never a supplied caller certificate. Single parent hBase is projected and reconstructed with identical S,e,U,T,Gamma,q,GammaP0,Inv,A0,B0,V0,R. Deleting only new D/semantics/intertwining block reproduces the complete parent Prop exactly.",
        "claim": "Same original caller and12 existential witnesses",
        "step": 1
      },
      {
        "audit": "ReflectionL2 is applied to the derived probability mu and original eta>0. Its U2 and parent U agree per observable with composition by the identical F on the same J. AE transitivity plus Lp.ext yields equality of quotient elements; LinearIsometry.ext gives U2=U. This uses no uniform null set or pointwise representative identity. The auxiliary rho is a kernel witness, not a new public premise.",
        "claim": "Same actual U, not a substitute reflection",
        "step": 2
      },
      {
        "audit": "Hperp is ker P with inherited Hilbert structure. D=R o U o inclusion maps all Hperp to Hperp; inclusion(Dh)=U(inclusion h)-P(U(inclusion h)) follows from existing hR. Ambient DA=Q U Q satisfies DA(inclusion h)=inclusion(Dh) because Ph=0. This is L2 equality, not an unproved pointwise identity. HP0 is the separate centered macroscopic kernel.",
        "claim": "Exact full micro-space compression",
        "step": 3
      },
      {
        "audit": "Use iota:HP0→ambient, BA iota u=inclusion(B0u), AJ iota u=iota(A0u), and ambient BA* DA=-AJ BA*. For arbitrary u:HP0,h:Hperp, <u,B0*Dh>=<BA iota u,DA h>=<iota u,BA*DA h>=-<AJ iota u,BA*h>=-<BA AJ iota u,h>=-<B0 A0u,h>=<u,-A0 B0*h>. The two selfadjoint transfers are AJ and A0; subspace inner products are inherited. ext_inner_left proves B0*D=-A0B0* for every h, with no onto V0/range restriction.",
        "claim": "B0-adjoint transport on all ker P",
        "step": 4
      },
      {
        "audit": "From the existing V0=B0 o Inv and Inv*=Inv on HP0, adjoint_comp gives V0*=Inv o B0*. Then V0*D=Inv(B0*D)=-Inv A0 B0*=-A0 Inv B0*=-A0 V0*, using SAME hCommInv in the symmetric direction. Inv is never extended to full HP or ambient L2. Neither full-perp isometry/coisometry nor onto V0 is asserted.",
        "claim": "Same centered inverse gives polar-adjoint identity",
        "step": 5
      },
      {
        "audit": "hGlobal is carried unchanged into hFinal and outer reconstruction. Its f is globally J-centered; fP is in exact HP0, fperp=Rf, fV=V0* fperp; ambient adjoint/root restriction, Pythagoras and contraction remain the original parent conclusions. The new identity does not replace the actual global-centering or conditional-kernel domains.",
        "claim": "All old global f conclusions retained",
        "step": 6
      },
      {
        "audit": "Only finite real Hilbert/Borel E,C2 V,0<alpha<=beta,two global Hessians,eta>0,beta eta<=1 occur in public caller. No Nontrivial,strict alpha eta<1,onto V0,H1,new root/gap/CFC/inverse/unit/energy/cost premise. Rank0 and alpha eta=1 are legal. Direct proof edges are actual67 and actualReflectionL2; sharp-energy68 is neither imported nor invoked. B21 projected rotation/corrector change,B4 dynamics,H1/main/invariance/nonexplosion/errors/caps/query costs/composition remain separate.",
        "claim": "Endpoints and dependency boundary",
        "step": 7
      }
